              "text": "మెచ్చుకో — meccukō — \"to appreciate; to praise\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నాన్న నా బొమ్మను మెచ్చుకున్నారు. nānna nā bommanu meccukunnāru. Dad praised my picture."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): మెచ్చుకున్నాను, meccukunnānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Warmer than పొగడు, which can be flattery: మెచ్చుకో (meccukō) is honest praise."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మెచ్చుకో (meccukō) is native Dravidian: DEDR 4722 lists Telugu meccu, \"to admire, to praise, to approve\", in the article of Tamil maruvu; -కో is the reflexive ending."
            }
          ]
        },
